  "tips": {
    "greetings": "💡 \"Namaste\" with pressed palms is universally understood and appreciated across India. English is widely spoken in cities.",
    "food": "💡 Ask \"Veg or non-veg?\" when ordering — many restaurants are pure vegetarian. Spice levels vary hugely by region.",
    "directions": "💡 Uber and Ola work well in cities. Auto-rickshaws should use meters — insist on it or agree on price before riding.",
    "numbers": "💡 Currency is Indian Rupees (₹). Bargaining is expected at markets but not in shops with price tags.",
    "emergency": "💡 Dial 112 (universal emergency). Tourist police helplines exist in major cities — save the local number.",
    "shopping": "Bargain in a bazaar. Pay the printed price in a shop.",
    "medical": "Call 112. Drink sealed bottled water, and skip ice you did not see poured.",
    "immigration": "Keep an offline copy of your e-visa and the first hotel address.",
    "hotel": "Ask whether the quoted rate includes tax. Use a padlock on a dorm locker.",
    "transport": "Use Uber or Ola, or agree the auto-rickshaw fare before you sit down."
  },
  "pronGuide": {
    "title": "Hindi Sounds",
    "tips": [
      "Hindi has retroflex consonants — T and D can be said with the tongue curled back (ट ड) vs forward (त द)",
      "The \"h\" after consonants (like \"bh\", \"dh\") adds a breathy puff of air",
      "Stress is generally on the second-to-last syllable",
      "The nasal anusvara (ं) nasalises the preceding vowel — like French nasal vowels"
    ]
  },
